# UpOnLAN — Operational Plan / Backlog

Ordered by priority. All remaining phases land on the `dev` branch, merged to `main` when complete.

## Phase 0 — Ship & unblock ✅ (done)

- [x] Merge `feat/helm-chart` → `main` (release pipeline, Helm chart, deploy hardening).
- [x] Fix the asset-release 2 GB bug (`iso_extraction` ISO cleanup in `release/assets/build.sh`).
- [x] Confirm the release runs — image ✓ release ✓ assets ✓.
- [x] Housekeeping — commit the `notes` deletion + this TODO.
- [x] Oracle decision → removed entirely (menu + assets + endpoints); menu `0.1.2`, webapp `1.0.2`.

## Phase 1 — Release pipeline hardening ✅ (done, on `dev`)

- [x] **ghcr login documented** — the package is private by default, so `podman login ghcr.io` is a documented prerequisite (can't flip visibility from the CLI token).
- [x] **Tag-triggered image** — `image.yml` builds on `push: tags: 'v*'` (version from the tag). The menu stays manual because its version lives in `version.ipxe`, decoupled from git tags.
- [x] **`assets.yml` per-OS target** — a `target` input; a targeted run merges its `endpoints.yml` into the existing catalog instead of overwriting it.
- [x] **Dropped the stale committed `release/assets/endpoints.yml`** — netboot-era and never consumed; the generated `release/output/assets/endpoints.yml` is the single catalog.

## Phase 2 — Menu/asset content → `dev`

- [x] **Rocky Linux local recipe** — `rocky8`/`rocky9` `direct_file` recipes; `rockylinux.ipxe` now boots `${mirror_endpoint}${asset_path}rocky-<ver>-<arch>/` (kernel+initrd re-hosted, `inst.repo` stays on the Rocky mirror).
- [x] **Provisioning profiles (Kickstart + cloud-init)**
  - **Milestones**
    - [x] **Phase 2A — backend + publish path**
    - [x] **Phase 2B — Menus-page authoring UI**
    - [x] **Phase 2C — Assets visibility + menu wiring + docs/tests**

## Phase 3 — Webapp features → `dev`

- [x] **Console: attach disks** — Create VM takes a disk size (GiB); a qcow2 volume is created in the libvirt `default` pool and attached as `vda` (0 = diskless). `vm:destroy` cleans it up.
- [x] **Wake-on-LAN** — show host status/IP + add a scheduler.

## Phase 4 — Platform hardening → `dev`
- [x] **Update Node.js** — Node 24 LTS (CI `20 → 24`; container already resolves 24.18.1; `engines: >=22 <27`).
- [x] **HTTPS** — nginx TLS termination (`:8443` assets, `:3443` webapp proxy), mounted cert or self-signed fallback; plain HTTP 8080/3000 stays for iPXE.
- [x] **Kubernetes** — chart renders `Deployment` (`deployAs: Deployment`, replicas 1) or the default `Pod`; Deployment mode drops `hostPort` + podman `emptyDir.path`; libvirt `hostPath` stays gated behind `libvirt.enabled`.

## Phase 5 — Polish → `dev`

- [x] **Prose brand sweep** — "UpOnLAN" → "UpOnLAN.xyz" in body text (URLs, `uponlan`, package name, and auth realm left unchanged).
- [x] **Repository endpoint setable** — documented `ENDPOINT_URL` (default `https://github.com/mozebaltyk/uponlan`) as the declarable repo endpoint (`menu.origin`).
- [x] **Docs** — ghcr private-fork login note; documented HTTPS-only boot + `inst.noverifyssl` for self-signed install sources.
